The UN Convention on the Rights of the Child was adopted in 1989 and became Swedish law in 2020. It establishes that the best interests of the child shall be a primary consideration in all actions concerning children.

In Swedish regulation the convention's principles appear, among other places, in work environment and fire safety contexts where young workers or children's safety is affected.
